# Documentation Rules

## General

Documentation should explain intent, behavior, constraints, and architectural decisions.

Do not document obvious code line-by-line.

## Architecture

When a significant architectural decision changes, update:

```text
docs/architecture.md
docs/decisions.md
```

when applicable.

## API

When an API contract changes, update:

```text
docs/api-contracts.md
```

and the OpenAPI/Swagger definition.

## Requirements

Do not silently change business requirements.

If implementation reveals an ambiguity or conflict, record it and resolve it before changing behavior.

## AI-Assisted Development

Before implementing a feature, inspect:

- `AGENTS.md`;
- relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`;
- relevant documents under `docs/`.

Do not invent requirements that are not documented.

When a requested implementation conflicts with an existing architectural rule, identify the conflict before coding.

## Comments

Comments should explain:

- why something is necessary;
- a non-obvious constraint;
- an external limitation;
- a deliberate architectural choice.

Avoid comments such as:

```python
# Increment counter
counter += 1
```
